{"agent":"impl-comp-ids","data":{"body":"Per D-completion-scope and the GENERIC rule: IDs come from the newest read-only .ddflow/index.db-* file; the record kinds that can be completed come from the RecordKind registry and the index tables (items, bugs, lessons, research, decisions, memories, prompts, rules ...), not a hand list, so a new record kind completes automatically. argcomplete starts ddflow on each TAB, so the completer path must not import ddflow.api (startup ~0.8 s): short-circuit before heavy imports and measure the budget. Falls back to nothing if no index; falsifier: if the budget cannot be met, report it to the operator.\n\nNote: ddflow/services/completion.py is an existing module, so a package completion/ would shadow it; the resolver lives at ddflow/services/completion_ids.py instead of completion/ids.py.","globs":["ddflow/services/completion_ids.py","ddflow/completion_fast.py","tests/test_completion_ids.py"]},"id":"e6ab3381892d66cd7fe9592bd","kind":"task.updated","lamport":116732,"schema":1,"subject":"COMP-ids-fast","ts":"2026-10-31T06:23:38.565763Z"}
